__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NOTICE_SHA256",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"NOTICE_TEXT",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const n="ba7cc3c812477783ce955723d73ff761b239a6c3abad30c1d2691e3f9b828987",t="OSlingo\nOperating-systems puzzles for CS 326 at USF, one small problem per screen.\n\nOSlingo's own code: license to be decided by the instructor.\n\nThis file lists the third-party work that OSlingo contains or is derived from,\nand the terms each one carries. Full license texts are in docs/licenses/.\nOSlingo is distributed free of charge.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n1. RustChap\n===============================================================================\n\nParts of OSlingo are derived from RustChap (https://github.com/unclecode/rustchap,\ncommit 5e9a80c). RustChap is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0,\nwith the Commons Clause License Condition v1.0. That condition requires every\nlicense notice or attribution to include it, so it is reproduced here verbatim:\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\"Commons Clause\" License Condition v1.0\n\nThe Software is provided to you by the Licensor under the License, as defined\nbelow, subject to the following condition.\n\nWithout limiting other conditions in the License, the grant of rights under\nthe License will not include, and the License does not grant to you, the right\nto Sell the Software.\n\nFor purposes of the foregoing, \"Sell\" means practicing any or all of the\nrights granted to you under the License to provide to third parties, for a fee\nor other consideration (including without limitation fees for hosting or\nconsulting/support services related to the Software), a product or service\nwhose value derives, entirely or substantially, from the functionality of the\nSoftware. Any license notice or attribution required by the License must also\ninclude this Commons Clause License Condition notice.\n\nSoftware: RustChap\nLicense: Apache License, Version 2.0\nLicensor: Hossein Tohidi (unclecode)\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe complete RustChap license (the condition above followed by the full text\nof the Apache License, Version 2.0) is in docs/licenses/RustChap-LICENSE.txt.\nThat file is a byte-for-byte copy of LICENSE at RustChap commit 5e9a80c.\n\nWhat OSlingo derives from RustChap:\n\n  Vendored source. It stays under RustChap's license. Files that OSlingo\n  changes carry a notice saying so (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)).\n    - crates/puzzle-schema   from RustChap crates/puzzle-schema\n                             (ops.rs, template.rs, validate.rs and the rest)\n    - crates/evaluator       from RustChap crates/evaluator\n    - tools/puzzle-linter    from RustChap tools/puzzle-linter\n                             (OSlingo change: Rust edition patched to 2021 to\n                             match the course crates)\n\n  TypeScript ports (packages/engine and apps/mobile), translated from\n  RustChap's Swift app at apps/ios/RustChap/:\n    - LocalEvaluator         Core/LocalEvaluator.swift\n    - Progression            Core/Progression.swift\n    - ProgressStore          Core/ProgressStore.swift (progress merge rules)\n    - ReviewStore            Core/ReviewStore.swift (review card states)\n    - ResumePoint            Core/ResumePoint.swift\n    - CostLanguage           Core/CostLanguage.swift (cost letters, live meter)\n    - RustLexer              PuzzleUI/RustLexer.swift\n    - The ops hash           crates/puzzle-schema/src/ops.rs (canonical ops\n                             JSON and its SHA-256), ported byte-for-byte\n\n  User-interface designs ported from RustChap's SwiftUI views:\n    - CodeSurface            PuzzleUI/CodeSurface.swift\n    - PuzzleScreen           Features/PuzzleScreen.swift\n    - ResultView             Features/ResultView.swift\n    - DeckListView           Features/DeckListView.swift\n\n  Formats, content and documents:\n    - The content contract (docs/CONTRACT.md) uses RustChap's puzzle,\n      lesson and outcomes formats (schemas/*.schema.json) as its base. The\n      slot-selection, minimal-edit and lesson shapes are used verbatim.\n    - Demo content adapted from RustChap's move-or-borrow.002 (\"Copy or\n      Move?\"). RustChap credits that puzzle as inspired by the rustlings\n      move_semantics and primitive_types exercises (rustlings, MIT License,\n      https://github.com/rust-lang/rustlings).\n    - docs/privacy.html and docs/support.html are adapted from RustChap's\n      docs/privacy.html and docs/index.html.\n    - The authoring house style (docs/authoring.md and\n      .claude/skills/oslingo-author/) is adapted from RustChap's\n      docs/context/foundation/curriculum.md and tools/prompts/deck-author.md.\n      Style and progression checks are adapted from tools/check-style.py and\n      tools/audit-progression.py.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n2. JetBrains Mono (font)\n===============================================================================\n\nOSlingo bundles JetBrains Mono NL (the variant without ligatures) for code.\n\n  Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors\n  (https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono)\n  License: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1\n  Full text: docs/licenses/JetBrainsMono-OFL-1.1.txt\n\nThe font is used unmodified and is not sold by itself.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n3. Lucide (icons)\n===============================================================================\n\nOSlingo's icons are drawn from Lucide (https://lucide.dev).\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Lucide Icons and Contributors\n  License: ISC License\n  Some Lucide icons are derived from Feather:\n  Copyright (c) 2013-present Cole Bemis, MIT License\n  Full text, including the list of Feather-derived icons:\n  docs/licenses/Lucide-ISC.txt\n\n\n===============================================================================\n4. Libraries and native code in the app\n===============================================================================\n\nThe app is built with Expo and React Native. Its iOS, Android and web builds\ncontain many open-source libraries, and native code compiled from other\nprojects. Each one keeps its own license and copyright lines.\n\nThe app lists every one of them under Settings > About > Licenses, grouped by\nlicense. Each entry shows its version, the platforms that include it and its\ncopyright lines. A license text that several entries share appears once, at\nthe top of its group. Any other license text, and any NOTICE or PATENTS file\nan entry carries, opens from that entry. docs/licenses/THIRD-PARTY.md holds\nthe same list as plain text.\n\nnpm run licenses:build makes both from what the builds contain. It reads the\nJavaScript bundles, the iOS pods and the Android release dependencies. Code\nthat one of those libraries copies from another project, such as the LLVM code\ninside Hermes, has an entry of its own.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n5. Tools used only at build time (nothing from them ships in the app)\n===============================================================================\n\n  TypeScript 6.0         Apache License 2.0, Microsoft Corp.\n  ajv 8                  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2015-2021 Evgeny Poberezkin\n  yaml 2                 ISC License, Copyright Eemeli Aro <eemeli@gmail.com>\n  Rust toolchain         MIT or Apache License 2.0, the Rust Project Developers\n  QEMU                   GPL-2.0. It runs as a separate program on the\n                         instructor's Mac to record bare-metal runs. The app\n                         ships only recorded results (console text, register\n                         and memory values), never QEMU code.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n6. Course material\n===============================================================================\n\nOSlingo's content is written for USF CS 326 from the course's own public\nmaterial (lecture and prep pages, the course schedule, guides and exercises),\nwith the instructor's permission. The app icon is the letters \"OS\" and a gold\nbar on flat green. The letters are outlines of JetBrains Mono NL Bold, the font\nin section 2. The icon uses no logos. The store listings say \"built for CS 326\nat USF\" in text only and use no USF logos."},833,[]);
